<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and two repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 1.208 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    350 days   20.67 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    182 days   20.54 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     91 days   19.33 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     35 days   19.00 pct</p>
<p>    158 million	1 day    18.09 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
